    "openingBoatFittingYardStandardPlating": "Yard-standard plating",
    "openingBoatFittingWhatABoatLeavesTheYardWith": "What a boat leaves the yard with: enough hull to hold pressure and take the knocks a crowded bay hands out. It is not armour and was never sold as any.",
    "openingBoatFittingReinforcedBellyPlate": "Reinforced belly plate",
    "openingBoatFittingASecondSkinLaidOverTheBelly": "A second skin laid over the belly and the cheeks, which is where a lander is hit on the way down. Every yard in the sector cuts these out of surplus plate; none of them will warrant the seams.",
    "openingBoatFittingArmouredLanderShell": "Armoured lander shell",
    "openingBoatFittingAssaultLanderPlateLaminateOverTheCrew": "Assault-lander plate, laminate over the crew spaces and the tanks. It costs the boat nothing but mass, and mass is the one thing a landing craft has least of — which is why it is bought by companies that expect to be shot at and nobody else.",
    "openingBoatFittingYardStandardDrive": "Yard-standard drive",
    "openingBoatFittingThePlantTheHullWasRatedFor": "The plant the hull was rated for. It lifts a full hold off the deck and puts it down again, at the pace the deck was built around.",
    "openingBoatFittingTunedDrive": "Tuned drive",
    "openingBoatFittingARefitCrewSWeekCleanFeed": "A refit crew's week: clean feed lines, re-cut nozzles, and the governor moved off the yard's cautious setting. Nothing exotic, and every hour of it shows on the descent.",
    "openingBoatFittingUpratedDrive": "Uprated drive",
    "openingBoatFittingABiggerPlantThanTheHullWas": "A bigger plant than the hull was drawn for, on mounts rebuilt to take it. It makes the boat quick enough to be somewhere else by the time the guns have settled, and it is not kind to the airframe.",
